<div style="padding:14px 26px 0;font:600 13px/1.4 'IBM Plex Mono',monospace;letter-spacing:.06em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#62707A">Wed, Jun 24</div>
<div style="display:flex;gap:8px;padding:12px 26px 4px;flex-wrap:wrap"><span style="font:700 11.5px/1 'Plus Jakarta Sans',sans-serif;letter-spacing:.04em;padding:6px 13px;border-radius:99px;background:#FFE9E6;color:#C2362A;opacity:.5">The Pulse</span><span style="font:700 11.5px/1 'Plus Jakarta Sans',sans-serif;letter-spacing:.04em;padding:6px 13px;border-radius:99px;background:#FFF2DC;color:#9A6206;box-shadow:0 0 0 2px #9A6206">Weekend</span><span style="font:700 11.5px/1 'Plus Jakarta Sans',sans-serif;letter-spacing:.04em;padding:6px 13px;border-radius:99px;background:#E4F4EC;color:#1F7A52;opacity:.5">Family</span></div>
<div style="padding:10px 26px 8px"><p style="font:400 15.5px/1.65 Inter,sans-serif;color:#3a4a53;margin:10px 0">The Fourth is a week out, but the fireworks start <em>this</em> weekend — three free shows — plus a final-season vineyard disco, a couple of long-awaited openings, free transit changes worth knowing, and youth-sports deadlines that close in days.</p>
<div style="font:800 12px/1 'Plus Jakarta Sans',sans-serif;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#FFB341;border-bottom:2px solid #FFB341;padding-bottom:8px;margin:30px 0 14px">This weekend</div>
<div style="font:800 12.5px/1.2 'Plus Jakarta Sans',sans-serif;letter-spacing:.10em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#FF5A47;margin:18px 0 6px">Fireworks, three ways</div>
<div style="margin:6px 0">
<div style="font:400 15.5px/1.6 Inter,sans-serif;color:#3a4a53;margin:7px 0;padding-left:14px;border-left:2px solid #e7e6e2"><strong style="color:#14272f"><a href="https://www.loudoun.gov/6019/Celebrate-Independence---Across-Your-Cou" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color:#3D9BD9;text-decoration:underline;font-weight:600">‘What a Blast!’ at Hanson Park</a> — Sat 6/27, 5–10pm, free.</strong> The big one, in Aldie (with Brambleton CA): The Legwarmers headline at 7, fireworks ~9:30 (rain date Sun 6/28). Kid's Zone, bounce houses, food trucks, splash pad. Free parking — lots fill by ~8pm, so come early.</div>
<div style="font:400 15.5px/1.6 Inter,sans-serif;color:#3a4a53;margin:7px 0;padding-left:14px;border-left:2px solid #e7e6e2"><strong style="color:#14272f"><a href="https://www.loudoun.gov/6019/Celebrate-Independence---Across-Your-Cou" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color:#3D9BD9;text-decoration:underline;font-weight:600">Star Spangled Sterling</a> — Fri 6/26, 6pm, fireworks 9:30.</strong> Sterling Middle School: DJ Greenzie, a Loudoun United FanZone, moonbounce, rock wall, food. Free.</div>
<div style="font:400 15.5px/1.6 Inter,sans-serif;color:#3a4a53;margin:7px 0;padding-left:14px;border-left:2px solid #e7e6e2"><strong style="color:#14272f"><a href="https://www.southriding.net/sr-events/star-spangled-south-riding/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color:#3D9BD9;text-decoration:underline;font-weight:600">Star Spangled South Riding</a> — Fri 6/26, 5:30–9:30pm.</strong> Parade at 5:30, Eclipse (a Journey tribute), fireworks ~9:15 at the golf club. (It's the 26th, not July 3rd — the Town moved it.) Coolers OK; no outside alcohol or pets.</div>
</div>
<div style="font:800 12.5px/1.2 'Plus Jakarta Sans',sans-serif;letter-spacing:.10em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#FF5A47;margin:18px 0 6px">Music &amp; shows</div>
<div style="margin:6px 0">
<div style="font:400 15.5px/1.6 Inter,sans-serif;color:#3a4a53;margin:7px 0;padding-left:14px;border-left:2px solid #e7e6e2"><strong style="color:#14272f"><a href="https://www.downtownoneloudoun.com/events/movie-nights-at-one-loudoun-2026" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color:#3D9BD9;text-decoration:underline;font-weight:600">Movie night: ‘Lilo &amp; Stitch’</a> at One Loudoun — Thu 6/25, 8pm, free.</strong> Outdoor screening with Alamo Drafthouse popcorn. (Fri 6/26: free Summer Strings with Roxanne Cook, 6–9.)</div>
<div style="font:400 15.5px/1.6 Inter,sans-serif;color:#3a4a53;margin:7px 0;padding-left:14px;border-left:2px solid #e7e6e2"><strong style="color:#14272f"><a href="https://www.downtownoneloudoun.com/events/summer-concert-series-2026-dm2jf" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color:#3D9BD9;text-decoration:underline;font-weight:600">Juniper Lights at One Loudoun</a> — Sat 6/27, 7–9pm, free.</strong> High-energy covers on the Plaza; all ages.</div>
<div style="font:400 15.5px/1.6 Inter,sans-serif;color:#3a4a53;margin:7px 0;padding-left:14px;border-left:2px solid #e7e6e2"><strong style="color:#14272f"><a href="https://www.tararaconcerts.com/schedule" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color:#3D9BD9;text-decoration:underline;font-weight:600">Groovalicious ’70s disco at Tarara</a> — Sat 6/27, 6–9:30 (gates 5).</strong> $20/$10 online. Bell-bottoms encouraged — and it's the Tarara Saturday series’ <em>final</em> season.</div>
<div style="font:400 15.5px/1.6 Inter,sans-serif;color:#3a4a53;margin:7px 0;padding-left:14px;border-left:2px solid #e7e6e2"><strong style="color:#14272f"><a href="https://vanishbeer.com/live-music/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color:#3D9BD9;text-decoration:underline;font-weight:600">Live music at Vanish Farmwoods Brewery</a> — Sat 6/27.</strong> Film at Eleven 1–4, Acoustic Chicks Band 5–8 at the big Leesburg farm-brewery; dogs and kids welcome.</div>
<div style="font:400 15.5px/1.6 Inter,sans-serif;color:#3a4a53;margin:7px 0;padding-left:14px;border-left:2px solid #e7e6e2"><strong style="color:#14272f"><a href="https://solacebrewing.com/events/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color:#3D9BD9;text-decoration:underline;font-weight:600">Solace pop-up at Halcyon Watson</a> (Leesburg) — Fri–Sun.</strong> Joel Delgado Fri 5–8, Berlin Calling (’80s) Sat 3–6, Ky Davis Sun 1–4; Solace beer + Paradise Springs wine, food trucks, free.</div>
<div style="font:400 15.5px/1.6 Inter,sans-serif;color:#3a4a53;margin:7px 0;padding-left:14px;border-left:2px solid #e7e6e2"><strong style="color:#14272f"><a href="https://tallyhotheater.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color:#3D9BD9;text-decoration:underline;font-weight:600">Tally Ho Theater</a> (downtown Leesburg).</strong> 90s Rockfest Fri 6/26, Better Off Dead (Dead tribute) Sat 6/27, a Taylor Swift singalong Sun 6/28 — doors 7 (Sun 6).</div>
</div>
<div style="font:800 12.5px/1.2 'Plus Jakarta Sans',sans-serif;letter-spacing:.10em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#FF5A47;margin:18px 0 6px">Just opened</div>
<div style="margin:6px 0">
<div style="font:400 15.5px/1.6 Inter,sans-serif;color:#3a4a53;margin:7px 0;padding-left:14px;border-left:2px solid #e7e6e2"><strong style="color:#14272f"><a href="https://www.anotherbrokenegg.com/locations/ashburn-va/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color:#3D9BD9;text-decoration:underline;font-weight:600">Another Broken Egg</a> — now serving at Bram Quarter (Ashburn).</strong> Brunch, 7am–2pm weekdays / 7am–3pm weekends. Expect a first-weekend wait.</div>
<div style="font:400 15.5px/1.6 Inter,sans-serif;color:#3a4a53;margin:7px 0;padding-left:14px;border-left:2px solid #e7e6e2"><strong style="color:#14272f"><a href="https://www.wonder.com/food-delivery-locations/sterling" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color:#3D9BD9;text-decoration:underline;font-weight:600">Wonder food hall</a> — grand opening Thu 6/25, Cascades Marketplace (Sterling).</strong> One kitchen, 20+ brands; order by app or kiosk.</div>
<div style="font:400 15.5px/1.6 Inter,sans-serif;color:#3a4a53;margin:7px 0;padding-left:14px;border-left:2px solid #e7e6e2"><strong style="color:#14272f">Also new around town:</strong> <a href="https://www.downtownoneloudoun.com/tatte" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color:#3D9BD9;text-decoration:underline;font-weight:600">Tatte Bakery</a> at One Loudoun, the new <a href="https://www.ikea.com/us/en/stores/chantilly/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color:#3D9BD9;text-decoration:underline;font-weight:600">IKEA in Chantilly</a>, and <a href="https://pinstackbowl.com/locations/kincora-loudoun-county-virginia/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color:#3D9BD9;text-decoration:underline;font-weight:600">Pinstack</a> bowling/arcade at Kincora — the latter two double as easy indoor backup plans.</div>
</div>
<div style="font:800 12px/1 'Plus Jakarta Sans',sans-serif;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#FF5A47;border-bottom:2px solid #FF5A47;padding-bottom:8px;margin:30px 0 14px">The Pulse</div>
<div style="margin:6px 0">
<div style="font:400 15.5px/1.6 Inter,sans-serif;color:#3a4a53;margin:7px 0;padding-left:14px;border-left:2px solid #e7e6e2"><strong style="color:#14272f">Free, expanded transit starts Wed 7/1.</strong> Loudoun launches a <a href="https://www.loudoun.gov/transit" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color:#3D9BD9;text-decoration:underline;font-weight:600">fare-free Transit On-Demand pilot</a> across a 14-sq-mile slice of Sterling and adds weekend on-demand service in Leesburg with four new pickup spots. Useful if you're car-light or commuting.</div>
<div style="font:400 15.5px/1.6 Inter,sans-serif;color:#3a4a53;margin:7px 0;padding-left:14px;border-left:2px solid #e7e6e2"><strong style="color:#14272f">Data Center Watch.</strong> Two things to know: data centers are <a href="https://www.loudoun.gov/5990/Data-Center-Standards-Locations" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color:#3D9BD9;text-decoration:underline;font-weight:600">no longer a "by-right" use anywhere in Loudoun</a> — every new project now needs public hearings (applications filed before Feb 12, 2025 are grandfathered). And supervisors are <a href="https://www.loudounnow.com/news/loudoun-supervisors-back-study-of-data-centers-at-gw-campus/article_6be2f193-9c41-4e52-9599-9a3d4e517e46.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color:#3D9BD9;text-decoration:underline;font-weight:600">studying the former GW campus off Route 7</a> (sold to Amazon for $427M) after vowing to fight centers that would harm neighbors. The corridor's defining fight.</div>
</div>
<div style="font:800 12px/1 'Plus Jakarta Sans',sans-serif;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#3FA776;border-bottom:2px solid #3FA776;padding-bottom:8px;margin:30px 0 14px">Family</div>
<div style="margin:6px 0">
<div style="font:400 15.5px/1.6 Inter,sans-serif;color:#3a4a53;margin:7px 0;padding-left:14px;border-left:2px solid #e7e6e2"><strong style="color:#14272f"><a href="https://library.loudoun.gov/SRP" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color:#3D9BD9;text-decoration:underline;font-weight:600">Summer Reading is the easy win</a>.</strong> The library's free 2026 program — "Dig into a prehistoric summer" — runs through Aug 16: finish 10 challenges for a free book and two Washington Nationals tickets, and every registrant gets a weekday kids' pass to Great Country Farms. Free dino family shows tour the branches (Dino Academy June 29–July 2).</div>
<div style="font:400 15.5px/1.6 Inter,sans-serif;color:#3a4a53;margin:7px 0;padding-left:14px;border-left:2px solid #e7e6e2"><strong style="color:#14272f"><a href="https://www.novaparks.com/parks/algonkian-regional-park" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color:#3D9BD9;text-decoration:underline;font-weight:600">Volcano Island Waterpark at Algonkian</a> is open weekends, 11am–7pm.</strong> Right in Ashburn's backyard — the easy weekend-with-kids move.</div>
<div style="font:400 15.5px/1.6 Inter,sans-serif;color:#3a4a53;margin:7px 0;padding-left:14px;border-left:2px solid #e7e6e2"><strong style="color:#14272f"><a href="https://www.loudounfarmersmarkets.org/markets" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color:#3D9BD9;text-decoration:underline;font-weight:600">Farmers markets</a>:</strong> Leesburg Sat 8–12, Cascades Sun 9–12; EatLoco at Ashbrook (Sat) and Brambleton (Sun), both 9–1.</div>
<div style="font:400 15.5px/1.6 Inter,sans-serif;color:#3a4a53;margin:7px 0;padding-left:14px;border-left:2px solid #e7e6e2"><strong style="color:#14272f"><a href="https://www.loudoun.gov/1202/Summer-Camps" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color:#3D9BD9;text-decoration:underline;font-weight:600">Summer camps</a>:</strong> county Daze/Fest camps (grades K–8) start the week of June 29 — check for open or late-add spots.</div>
</div>
<div style="font:800 12px/1 'Plus Jakarta Sans',sans-serif;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#FF5A47;border-bottom:2px solid #FF5A47;padding-bottom:8px;margin:30px 0 14px">Registration radar</div>
<div style="margin:6px 0">
<div style="font:400 15.5px/1.6 Inter,sans-serif;color:#3a4a53;margin:7px 0;padding-left:14px;border-left:2px solid #e7e6e2"><strong style="color:#14272f">Youth football — <a href="https://www.clyfl.org/tacklefootball" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color:#3D9BD9;text-decoration:underline;font-weight:600">CLYFL fall tackle closes Sat 6/27</a>.</strong> Most divisions are full; grades 5–6 still open. Proof-of-grade and physicals due July 1.</div>
<div style="font:400 15.5px/1.6 Inter,sans-serif;color:#3a4a53;margin:7px 0;padding-left:14px;border-left:2px solid #e7e6e2"><strong style="color:#14272f">Basketball — <a href="https://www.ashburnathleticassociation.com/dulles-youth-basketball.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color:#3D9BD9;text-decoration:underline;font-weight:600">Dulles Youth Basketball opens July 1</a></strong> (grades K–5; $200, rises to $250 after Sept 1).</div>
<div style="font:400 15.5px/1.6 Inter,sans-serif;color:#3a4a53;margin:7px 0;padding-left:14px;border-left:2px solid #e7e6e2"><strong style="color:#14272f">Soccer — <a href="https://www.loudounsoccer.com/rec-programs" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color:#3D9BD9;text-decoration:underline;font-weight:600">Loudoun Soccer fall rec is open</a></strong> (closes Aug 7; players placed first-registered).</div>
<div style="font:400 15.5px/1.6 Inter,sans-serif;color:#3a4a53;margin:7px 0;padding-left:14px;border-left:2px solid #e7e6e2"><strong style="color:#14272f">Watch for it:</strong> the county's <a href="https://www.loudoun.gov/2448/Activity-Guide" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color:#3D9BD9;text-decoration:underline;font-weight:600">Fall Activity Guide</a> drops online mid-July — the trigger for most fall rec programs.</div>
<div style="font:400 15.5px/1.6 Inter,sans-serif;color:#3a4a53;margin:7px 0;padding-left:14px;border-left:2px solid #e7e6e2"><strong style="color:#14272f">Soccer fans:</strong> no Loudoun United home match this weekend; next at Segra Field is <a href="https://www.loudoununitedfc.com/schedule/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color:#3D9BD9;text-decoration:underline;font-weight:600">Fri 7/3, 7pm vs Sporting JAX</a> ("703 Night").</div>
</div>
<div style="font:800 12px/1 'Plus Jakarta Sans',sans-serif;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#FF5A47;border-bottom:2px solid #FF5A47;padding-bottom:8px;margin:30px 0 14px">The week ahead — July 4th</div>
<div style="margin:6px 0">
<div style="font:400 15.5px/1.6 Inter,sans-serif;color:#3a4a53;margin:7px 0;padding-left:14px;border-left:2px solid #e7e6e2">The county slate runs Fri 6/26–Sat 7/4. Standouts: <strong style="color:#14272f"><a href="https://www.leesburgva.gov/departments/parks-recreation/events/independence-day" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color:#3D9BD9;text-decoration:underline;font-weight:600">Leesburg's celebration</a></strong> (Sat 7/4 — parade 10am downtown, then the region's largest fireworks at Ida Lee, 9:30), <strong style="color:#14272f"><a href="https://www.loudoun.gov/6019/Celebrate-Independence---Across-Your-Cou" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color:#3D9BD9;text-decoration:underline;font-weight:600">Fourth Fest at Claude Moore</a></strong> (Sat 7/4, 10:30am–3pm family day), <strong style="color:#14272f">Franklin on the Fourth</strong> fireworks, and <strong style="color:#14272f">Lovettsville's</strong> parade + fireworks Fri 7/3. Full rundown next week.</div>
</div>
